### SADC Order Management: example requests
### Works with the VS Code REST Client extension, Visual Studio 2022 and JetBrains Rider.
### Run the requests top to bottom: later requests reuse values captured by earlier ones.

# Visual Studio / dotnet run (http profile). For Docker Compose use http://localhost:5080
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5059

### 0. Health and reference data (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/readiness

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reference/sadc-countries

### 1. Get a mock token (Auth:Mode = Mock only). Roles: Orders.Read, Orders.Write, Orders.Admin
# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roles": ["Orders.Read", "Orders.Write", "Orders.Admin"] }

###
@auth = Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Create a customer (201 + Location)
# @name customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: demo-create-customer-001

{ "name": "Tendai Moyo", "email": "tendai.{{$randomInt 1000 99999}}@example.zw", "countryCode": "ZW" }

###
@customerId = {{customer.response.body.id}}

### 3. Validation error: non-SADC country -> 400 with errors.countryCode
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Amara", "email": "amara@example.ke", "countryCode": "KE" }

### 4. Get / search customers (pageSize <= 100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: {{auth}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers?search=moyo&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: {{auth}}

### 5. Create an order (ZW allows ZWL, USD and ZWG). The server computes TotalAmount and OrderCreated goes to the outbox.
# @name order
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "currencyCode": "USD",
  "lineItems": [
    { "productSku": "SOLAR-LAMP", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 24.99 },
    { "productSku": "SEED-PACK", "quantity": 10, "unitPrice": 3.10 }
  ]
}

###
@orderId = {{order.response.body.id}}

### 6. Currency not allowed for the customer's country -> 400 errors.currencyCode
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}", "currencyCode": "ZAR", "lineItems": [ { "productSku": "X", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1 } ] }

### 7. Get the order. Copy the ETag into If-None-Match and send again to get 304.
# @name getOrder
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: {{auth}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
If-None-Match: {{getOrder.response.headers.ETag}}

### 8. List orders: filter, sort, paginate
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?customerId={{customerId}}&status=Pending&sort=-totalAmount&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: {{auth}}

### 9. Idempotent status change. Send it twice: the second response has "Idempotent-Replayed: true".
# (The worker may already have fulfilled the order. If so you get a 409 with allowedTransitions.)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 4b1d1c9e-demo-key-0001

{ "status": "Cancelled" }

### 10. Same key, different body -> 422 idempotency_key_reused
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 4b1d1c9e-demo-key-0001

{ "status": "Paid" }

### 11. Missing Idempotency-Key -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Paid" }

### 12. No token -> 401 Problem Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders

### 13. Basic metrics
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics
